# Every path is owned by the maintainer. The explicit entries below change no
# ownership — `*` already matches everything — they exist so that a change to a
# gate file asks for review by name instead of slipping through on a green CI.
#
# A gate file is one whose contents decide whether other changes pass:
# `docs/change-rules.md` § 1. Changing one re-runs both sides' checks.

*                       @imrajmishraa

# CI and the gates
/.github/               @imrajmishraa
/scripts/               @imrajmishraa
/client/scripts/        @imrajmishraa
/server/scripts/        @imrajmishraa
/docs/change-rules.md   @imrajmishraa
/AGENTS.md              @imrajmishraa
/CLAUDE.md              @imrajmishraa
/DESIGN.md              @imrajmishraa
/docs/constraints.md    @imrajmishraa

# Security and deployment
/SECURITY.md            @imrajmishraa
/render.yaml            @imrajmishraa
/docker-compose.yml     @imrajmishraa
/server/vercel.json     @imrajmishraa
/server/Dockerfile      @imrajmishraa

# Dependency surface: a new lockfile is a new supply chain
**/package.json         @imrajmishraa
**/package-lock.json    @imrajmishraa
**/.env.example         @imrajmishraa
